{"id":"tuido-229065","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:24:21.741101Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"tuido-2170e7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Atomic save replaces a symlinked todos.json with a regular file","description":"Found while speccing tuido-229065, whose use case is a todo file in a synced folder.\n\n`storage::save_todos` writes `todos.json.tmp` next to the path and then `rename`s it over the path. If `todos.json` is a **symlink**, for example `~/.config/tuido/todos.json -\u003e ~/Dropbox/todos.json`, the rename replaces the symlink itself with a regular file. From then on tuido writes to the local copy, and the synced file silently stops updating.\n\nA second, smaller problem: the temp file is named with `with_extension(\"json.tmp\")`, so a custom file such as `todo.txt` gets a temp file called `todo.json.tmp`.\n\n**Fix**\n- In `save_todos`, resolve the target through symlinks (`fs::canonicalize` when the file exists), and write the temp file next to the real file before renaming it over the real file.\n- Name the temp file by appending `.tmp` to the full file name.\n\n**Test:** saving through a symlink keeps the symlink and updates its target. This needs a Unix-only test, gated with `#[cfg(unix)]`.\n\nFixed as part of tuido-229065.","sort_order":"a6","dependencies":[{"source_id":"tuido-2170e7","target_id":"tuido-229065","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:25:20.018933Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
